      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It sucks cause I noticed that issue when testing the Open Beta branch, I honestly thought they would fix that before pulling that update to everyone,\n\nI was alright with all formers update but this one I got a very bad opinion of it;\n\nWrist Angle like you said is different, it infuriates me a lot because even trying to re-adjust the wrist angle in the existing slider setting, it's not entirely perfect because it is offset on the position.\n\nDefault triggers sensitivity on quest touch controllers are WAY too high (70% pressed) which makes hard for peoples to press buttons on the UI.\n\nRadial Menu prevents you to move unless you have One Handed Mode enabled.\n\nIf there was a way to revert to the previous version I would gladly do.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
